Language English

Book CloseGate Ordered No Keep Looped
    Triggered By @ReadDvm If goal = goalCloseGate And firstRitual = firstRitualOver

    // this hides the page since we are NO Keep
    // this is easier than managing visibility
    if Not closeGateInitialized Then Mark Step2Repeat Read
	closeGateInitialized = true
	
	Page Init
		Text """
			Matthias looks up and flings an arm in your direction and...
			something happens. Each investigator except {c:EventChosenInvestigator}
			becomes Restrained.
			
			Sarah says to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<You must stop Matthias
			and seal the gate. Only you can do it.>>
		"""
		
		Exit
	End Page
	
    Page Step1
        Prolog """
            The gate is open and you must close it quickly. Only
			{c:EventChosenInvestigator} can perform this ritual and only while
			standing at the altar.
        
            Are you ready?
        """

        Button "Begin Ritual"

        Text """
            You flip to the correct place in the book, turn to face the altar,
			and lay out the materials. The pattern is complex and it takes a
			few minutes to get right. Your companions are under constant attack
			by cult members and you can feel the approach of something from the
			other side of the gate. You must hurry.
    
            Drop the {c:QItemRitualComponents} Unique Item on the altar. It
			must stay on the altar for the duration of the ritual.
    
            This step is complete.
        """
    End Page Step1

    Page Step2
        Prolog """
            You turn the page and again review the process for <<blessing>> the
			knife. When you glance down, you are surprised that you can read the
            words now.

            You pull out the {c:QItemRitualDagger} and...
        """

        Button "Prepare the knife"

        Text """
            The book shows you how to hold the knife and some kind movement,
			like you're presenting it to the altar. You fumble around, hoping
			your first try at something like this will be good enough.

            While you can read the words, you aren't sure you understand them.
            If you do, test {lore}; otherwise, test {will} and hope for the
			best.
        
            For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
        """
		
		// even if we pass, we fail
        Test Quota 10 set passWhoCares
        Goto Step2Fail
    End Page Step2

    Page Step2Pass
        Not Visible

        Text """
            As you finish the incantation, the blade becomes heavier and
			brighter. It... changes. The {c:QItemRitualKnife} is ready for
			what comes next.
        
            This step is complete
        """
    End Page Step2Pass

    Page Step2Fail
        Not Visible

        Text """
            You finish the incantation but nothing seems to have happened.
			You'll need to keep trying.
        
            Suffer 1 facedown Damage and 1 facedown Horror ({will} negates).
        """

        Mark Step2Repeat Unread
    End Page Step2Fail

    Page Step2Repeat
        Text """
            The knife still feels cold and dead in your hand. You're starting
			to wonder if you>'ll really be able to do this. You look at your
			fellow investigators, struggling to keep you alive and look down
			to try again.
*			
            You squeeze more blood out of your fist on to the {c:QItemElderSign}.
			As you do, you speak the words again.

            Test {lore} or {will}.
        
            For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
        """

        Test Quota 4 Set passCloseGateStep5
        If passCloseGateStep5 Then Goto Step5Pass
        Goto Step5Fail
    End Page Step2Repeat

	Page SarahTransports
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @AnotherRequirementCompleted If goal = goalCloseGate And foundDagger And foundDvm And foundElderSign And exploredDungeonCell And exploredCryptViaChapel And exploredDungeonCaveViaBasement
		
		Text """
			Sarah smiles for the first time and says out load, <<That's it! Now
			we know what is going on, where Mathias is working, and what to do about
			it. I think I can take us where we need to be.>>
			
			Sarah seems to grow, getting more transparent. Suddenly, the world
			shifts and you are... somewhere else. And disoriented. There is
			noise and light and someone yelling. Folks are rushing by. It all
			seems far away.>>
		"""
		
		If firstRitual < firstRitualWoman Call MythosFirstRitualFeedOrCloseGate.Woman
		If firstRitual < firstRitualOpenGate Call MythosFirstRitualFeedOrCloseGate.OpenGate
		
		firstRitual = false
		Trigger @ExploreAltarViaSarah
		Goto Init
	End Page SarahTransports
End CloseGate